question:
What is printed by the following string equality checks?
```java
String s1 = "Hello";
String s2 = "Hello";
String s3 = new String("Hello");
System.out.println((s1 == s2) + " " + (s1 == s3));
```

What is the output after calling `.intern()` in the following snippet?
```java
String s1 = new String("Java");
String s2 = s1.intern();
String s3 = "Java";
System.out.println((s1 == s3) + " " + (s2 == s3));
```

What is the output of the following code involving `final` string variables?
```java
final String str1 = "Java";
final String str2 = "8";
String str3 = str1 + str2;
String str4 = "Java8";
System.out.println(str3 == str4);
```

What is the output if `str1` and `str2` are NOT final in the previous scenario?
```java
String str1 = "Java";
String str2 = "8";
String str3 = str1 + str2;
String str4 = "Java8";
System.out.println(str3 == str4);
```

What is printed by the following code?
```java
String s = "Java";
s.concat(" SE");
System.out.println(s);
```

What is the output of the following `StringBuilder` snippet?
```java
StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("Java");
sb.append("17").insert(4, "-");
System.out.println(sb);
```
